# A constant must fit where it lands, as any value must. A named untyped
# constant passed to a u8 parameter at unit level must fit u8, as the literal
# it names must; a typed constant there converts or is refused, and is not
# also range-checked as a literal. `.or d:` on an option constant holding
# nothing is the default as the payload's type, so adding to it can overflow
# that type. A list element out of the element type's range is refused once,
# whether written or folded, and a later read of it is not refused again.
small: function {v: u8} out u8 is {
    return v
}

K: 300
X: (small v: K)
N: 300.u16
Y: (small v: N)
G: "hello"
PAST: ((G.byteAt 100).or d: 7)
Z: PAST + 250
two: 2
codes: list { a: 300  b: (two * 200) } out staticlist u8

main: function is {
    n: codes.a + 1
    m: codes.b + 1
    print "\{X} \{Y} \{Z} \{n} \{m}"
}
